+<a name="mixed"></a>
+<h4>Mixed Normative content</h4>
+<p>
+Standards status can be assigned to individual artifacts and, where explicitly labeled, to individual parts of an artifact. A
+Normative artifact may therefore contain elements or sections that remain <i>Trial Use</i>. These parts are clearly labeled in
+the resource definitions or page content, and may change under the rules that apply to Trial Use content.
+</p>
+<p>
+Conversely, a Trial Use artifact may include Normative content inherited from or reused by more mature artifacts. For example,
+Trial Use resources still include Normative content from <a href="resource.html">Resource</a>,
+<a href="domainresource.html">DomainResource</a>, and the <a href="datatypes.html">Datatypes</a>.
+</p>
+<p>
+Operations and profiles that use a resource have their own FMM levels. They may have a lower maturity level than the resource or
+resources they reference, but cannot have a higher maturity level than those resources.
+</p>
